# ─── Secrets (NEVER commit) ──────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── Go build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
coverage.out
*.cover
# Stray binaries from `go build ./cmd/<name>` (without -o) — same
# names as the cmd dirs. /bin/ catches `make build`, these catch
# ad-hoc builds.
/api
/worker
/expiration-watcher
/dashboard-server
/mintjwt
/seed-inventory

# ─── Vendored deps (we don't vendor; module cache only) ───────
/vendor/

# ─── Build output directory ───────────────────────────────────
# Created by `go build -o bin/<name> ./cmd/<name>`; never commit
# the compiled binaries.
/bin/

# ─── Transient dev scripts (older smoke-test helpers) ────────
# The old scripts/mintjwt.go had a hardcoded secret; it was promoted to
# cmd/mintjwt/main.go so the secret could be env-driven. The .go file is
# still on disk (user deletes manually per the no-rm safety rule) but
# must never be committed. The .sh files in scripts/ ARE tracked
# (start-bg.sh / stop-bg.sh are real dev tooling used by the Makefile).
/scripts/*.go

# ─── Editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# ─── k6 / load test artifacts ────────────────────────────────
loadtest/results/
*.json.gz
summary.html

# ─── Runtime logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
